    <p class="lede first reveal">Here is the quiet truth about AI and your business: the tool is not the hard part. You already have access to the same models everyone else does. What separates the woman whose business feels lighter every month from the one still doing everything by hand is not a better tool — it is a better relationship with the one she already has.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Most women open an AI model, type a vague request, get back something generic, and quietly conclude the technology is overhyped. They are not wrong about what they got. They are wrong about why. The problem was never the machine. It was that no one ever taught them how to ask.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>You do not have a technology problem. You have a delegation problem.</strong> AI is the first assistant you will ever manage — and like any assistant, it is only as good as the brief you hand it. Once you learn to brief it well, whole afternoons of your week come back.</p>

