    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">01</span><div class="num">Chapter One</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="does">What AI actually does for a one-woman business</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">For a small online business, AI does one thing well: it takes the repetitive thinking work — drafting, summarising, structuring, reformatting — off your plate so your hours go to the decisions only you can make.</p>
    <p class="reveal">It is not a strategist and it is not a founder. It will not tell you what to sell or who to serve. What it will do is take a decision you have already made and carry out the labour around it at a speed no human assistant could match. You decide the newsletter's angle; it drafts three versions. You choose the product; it writes the sales page. You set the direction; it handles the miles.</p>
    <div class="box tip reveal"><span class="tag"><span class="g">✦</span> The Edit</span><p>The clearest way to think about AI: it is not a search engine and it is not magic. It is a very fast, very literal assistant who has read almost everything and remembers none of your context unless you give it. Treat it that way and it stops disappointing you.</p></div>

