    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">02</span><div class="num">Chapter Two</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="vending">The vending machine problem</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">Most women get little back from AI because they use it like a vending machine — one short request in, one generic result out — instead of like a hire they brief, correct, and direct.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Picture how you would treat a real assistant on their first day. You would not walk past their desk, say "write me something for Instagram," and expect brilliance. You would tell them who the brand is, who you are talking to, what has worked before, and what you are trying to make happen. <strong>AI needs exactly that, every single time, because it starts every conversation with no memory of you.</strong></p>

