    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">04</span><div class="num">Chapter Four</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="brief">How to brief AI like you'd brief a hire</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">Brief AI the way you'd brief a new hire: tell it who it is, who it's talking to, what you want, and what "good" looks like. Those four things turn a generic result into a usable one.</p>
    <p class="reveal">There is no secret phrasing and no magic word. A good brief is just complete. When something comes back flat, the fix is almost never a cleverer prompt — it is a fuller one.</p>

    <div class="framework reveal">
      <span class="tag"><span>✦</span> The Four-Part Brief</span>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="node"><div class="h">Role</div><div class="t">Who it should be — "a warm email copywriter for a faceless brand."</div></div>
        <div class="arrow">→</div>
