    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">05</span><div class="num">Chapter Five</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="stops">Where AI stops and you start</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">AI stops at judgement. It can draft, summarise, and structure — but the taste to know what's good, the decisions about direction, and the final word before anything ships stay with you.</p>
    <p class="reveal">This is not a limitation to work around. It is the line that keeps your brand yours. A model can generate a hundred captions; only you know which one sounds like you. It can outline a launch; only you know whether now is the right time. <strong>AI is the fastest hands you'll ever have. You are still the head.</strong></p>

    <div class="box mistake reveal"><span class="tag"><span class="g">✕</span> Common Mistake</span><p>Publishing what AI writes without reading it as the editor. The draft is the starting line, never the finish. The moment your audience can tell a machine wrote it unattended is the moment the trust you're building quietly leaks away.</p></div>

    <div class="marginal reveal">
      <p>A simple test before anything goes out: <em>would you have said it this way?</em> If not, it isn't done — it's a draft waiting for your hand.</p>
      <span class="note">taste is the thing they can't automate ✶</span>
    </div>

    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">06</span><div class="num">Chapter Six</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="workflow">Building your first repeatable AI workflow</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">A repeatable AI workflow is a saved brief you reuse: one clear set of instructions for a task you do often, so you're never writing the prompt from scratch again.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The women who get the most from AI are not writing brilliant new prompts every day. They wrote a good one once, saved it, and now they just swap in this week's topic. That is the whole trick — turn your best brief into a template and stop starting over.</p>

    <div class="notebook reveal">
