    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">Which AI tool should a beginner start with?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Either of the two major conversational models — ChatGPT or Claude — is more than enough to start. Both have a free tier that covers everything in this guide. Pick one, learn to brief it well, and don't let tool-hopping become another way to avoid starting.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">Will AI make my brand sound generic?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Only if you let it write unattended. AI sounds generic when it's given nothing to work with. Give it your voice, your reader, and your edit at the end, and it becomes a way to produce more of what already sounds like you — not less.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">Do I need to know anything technical?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">No. If you can write a clear set of instructions to a capable assistant, you can use AI for your business. The skill is not technical — it's the ability to explain what you want clearly, and that's a skill you already have.</p>

